    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><em>“You can stitch courage into the air itself.”</em></p><p>When you or an ally you can see within <strong>6 squares</strong> succeeds on an attack roll, defense check, or attribute check by <strong>5 or more</strong>, you can use your <strong>reaction</strong> to declare a surge of momentum.</p><ul><li>Allies of your choice within <strong>3 squares</strong> gain <strong>temporary Integrity equal to your tier</strong>.</li><li>Those allies also gain a <strong>+2 squares bonus</strong> to their speed until the end of their next turn.</li><li>The next <strong>Diplomacy (Presence)</strong> or <strong>Intimidation (Presence)</strong> check made by any one of the affected creatures before the end of the scene has <strong>advantage</strong>.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your <strong>tier</strong>, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Soma Break.</p><p><strong>OP Echo.</strong> If a Triumph Weave directly helps resolve a conflict without lethal force, your faction gains <strong>+1 Diplomacy OP</strong> for the next strategic turn.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
